From 2424c446a10a078eee1ae2fcfbfb06ae01c5706a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:42:05 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 18/31] arm64: dts: apple: t6050: share the G17C GPU
 description

The M5 Max GPU description in t6050-j716c-gpu-panel.dtsi (the GPU node under
/soc@2300000000, its mailboxes, reservations, operating point tables and
GPU power states) has nothing J716c-specific in it: every value is either
the SoC's or left zero for the loader to fill from the ADT.

Move that half into t6050-gpu-g17c.dtsi and include it from the J716c file,
which keeps the internal panel half. Let a board that has no GPU bus of its
own ask t6050-peripherals.dtsi for one with T6050_GPU_BUS, so the GPU PMGR
lands under /soc@2300000000 where the loader looks for it, as on J716c.

No functional change: no board defines T6050_GPU_BUS yet and the J716c DTB is
byte-identical before and after.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
