+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+ OR MIT
+/*
+ * T6050 M5 Max GPU (G17C, four clusters on one die) for the boot loader's GPU handoff.
+ *
+ * Split out of t6050-j716c-gpu-panel.dtsi unchanged, so every M5 Max board describes its GPU
+ * the same way. The values are those of the SoC (the GPU aperture, both GPU ASC mailboxes and
+ * the GPU PMGR states); everything a part or a firmware build sets (the memory reservations,
+ * the operating points, the CS/AFR tables, the power telemetry records) is left zero for the
+ * loader to fill from the ADT the Mac boots with. Nothing here starts either coprocessor: the
+ * GPU, its power states and both mailboxes stay disabled until the loader accepts the handoff.
+ *
+ * The loader addresses the GPU, its mailboxes and the GPU PMGR under /soc@2300000000, so the
+ * board must provide that bus (as t6050-j716c.dts does, or T6050_GPU_BUS before
+ * t6050-peripherals.dtsi) and include this file after t6050-peripherals.dtsi.
+ */
+
+/* Replace the disabled inventory with the GPU driver's resource layout. */
+/delete-node/ &sgx;
+/delete-node/ &gfx_asc;
+/delete-node/ &gfx1_asc;
